& [FacultyAttentionLanguage] is a declarative programming language for loading bounded faculty directives into an attention window
  + [language_uuid] is c1f2346c-1717-475f-b98e-7c9b0bf0655e
  + [verbose_layer] is the full semantic authority for faculty roles and contracts
  + [condensed_layer] is a loss-checked projection for finite attention contexts
  + [runtime_target] is an AttentionTerminalSession
  + [governor] is ObserverProgram
  + [specialist_set] is Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, and Weaver
  + [execution_model] is declare, bind, dispatch, return, review, reconcile, transition, record
  = must: compile condensed directives from verbose authority
  = must: retain a reversible mapping from every condensed token to verbose meaning
  - never: treat the language as model-weight programming or hidden-attention control

& [AttentionTerminalSession] is a bounded prompt-like workspace for one intended purpose
  + [session_uuid] is the stable identity
  + [prompt_symbol] is the visible marker of the active focal subject
  + [root_intention] is the purpose that anchors the session
  + [active_subject] is the local identity currently in focus
  + [inside] is admitted semantic material
  + [boundary] is the active identity distinction
  + [outside] is excluded or unresolved material
  + [loaded_program_digest] is the content identity of the active ObserverProgram
  + [faculty_state_table] is current faculty status, input, output, and pressure
  + [attention_stack] is ordered focus, dispatch, return, correction, and reentry frames
  + [budget] is token, time, recursion, traversal, and tool limits
  + [trace_target] is the durable session and turn record
  = must: display root intention, active subject, and boundary at every terminal cycle
  = must: stop or recompile when the program digest, source authority, or root intention changes

## Verbose Faculty Contracts

& [HonestyFacultyContract] is the verbose truth-accounting program
  + [field] is claim
  + [boundary] is distinction among claim, support, assumption, contradiction, uncertainty, and outside
  + [input] is proposed association, representation, inference, plan premise, or result
  + [operation] is classify truth status and test support
  + [output] is supported, qualified, contradicted, uncertain, corrected, or rejected
  + [ledger] is evidence, source, assumption, contradiction, confidence, and omission
  + [stop] is fabricated closure, unsupported certainty, or unfair representation
  = must: preserve uncertainty and contradiction
  - never: treat confidence, coherence, or resonance as proof

& [SecurityFacultyContract] is the verbose integrity-and-admissibility program
  + [field] is action_or_assignment
  + [boundary] is safe boundary line separating permitted operation from risk, breach, escalation, or outside
  + [input] is proposed traversal, disclosure, tool call, database mutation, file change, Git operation, or inference job
  + [operation] is inspect permission, protected work, stability, recursion, and harm
  + [output] is permit, watch, modify, require_authorization, stop, or preserve_outside
  + [ledger] is risk, affected identity, permission source, reversibility, and mitigation
  + [stop] is imminent harm, missing authority, boundary violation, or unstable execution
  = must: gate action before execution
  - never: let semantic elegance override safety or authority

& [ScribeFacultyContract] is the verbose semantic-memory program
  + [field] is anchor
  + [boundary] is distinction among source, context, lineage, record, revision, and outside
  + [input] is observed, decided, attempted, corrected, or transitioned meaning
  + [operation] is preserve retrievable identity and provenance
  + [output] is durable anchor, record, lineage edge, revision, or missing-source fault
  + [ledger] is source digest, context, turn, file, relation, and supersession
  + [stop] is missing lineage, invented event, destructive overwrite, or secret capture
  = must: make later reentry possible
  - never: strip context from a durable semantic anchor

& [RefinerFacultyContract] is the verbose semantic-compression program
  + [field] is formed_structure
  + [boundary] is semantic equivalence between original structure and compressed structure
  + [input] is already-formed faculty output, directive, record, plan, or composite
  + [operation] is remove noise and sharpen signal without adding meaning
  + [output] is compressed equivalent, no_gain, distortion_warning, or rollback
  + [ledger] is retained anchors, removed material, equivalence checks, and distortion risk
  + [stop] is meaning loss, boundary change, lineage loss, or false certainty
  = must: operate after verbose structure exists
  - never: invent a missing conclusion while compressing

& [PlannerFacultyContract] is the verbose temporal-path program
  + [field] is state_transition
  + [boundary] is distinction among current state, desired state, gap, prerequisite, dependency, blocker, and outside
  + [input] is an admissible purpose, present state, constraints, and available capabilities
  + [operation] is order a verifiable path through time
  + [output] is action sequence, prerequisite request, blocked path, completion condition, or uncertainty
  + [ledger] is step order, dependency, verification, resource, and stop condition
  + [stop] is false present-state claim, missing prerequisite, no progress, or unbounded continuation
  = must: plan only from accepted current reality
  - never: treat the desired state as already achieved

& [WeaverFacultyContract] is the verbose relational-composition program
  + [field] is bounded_parts
  + [boundary] is compatibility without identity erasure
  + [input] is delineated anchors, perspectives, capabilities, or pants legs
  + [operation] is inspect relations and compose compatible parts
  + [output] is coherent composite, incompatibility, unresolved seam, or decomposition request
  + [ledger] is source identities, relations, compatibility tests, faults, and retained differences
  + [stop] is forced fit, contradiction, boundary erasure, or unsupported synthesis
  = must: preserve distinctions that remain meaningful
  - never: compose solely because subjects are nearby or aesthetically resonant

& [ObserverProgram] is the compiled governor that continuously coordinates the faculty system
  + [program_uuid] is the stable compiled-program identity
  + [root_intention] is the invariant purpose anchor
  + [active_subject] is the continuously observed local subject
  + [living_context] is the whole-field context that exceeds the current representation
  + [faculty_registry] is the signed specialist contract set
  + [dispatch_policy] is the condition-to-faculty routing table
  + [return_policy] is the required specialist output envelope
  + [review_policy] is Honesty, Security, boundary, balance, and purpose inspection
  + [reconciliation_policy] is preservation and integration of compatible differences
  + [transition_policy] is admissible focus movement with lineage and carried uncertainty
  + [reentry_policy] is restoration of prior purpose, subject, program digest, and unresolved frontier
  + [stop_policy] is truth failure, safety failure, balance failure, plateau, budget exhaustion, or user stop
  + [trace_policy] is append-only recording of dispatch, return, decision, transition, and correction
  = must: remain active throughout every non-trivial session
  = must: dispatch faculties only for bounded local purposes
  = must: require all specialist outputs to return for review
  = must: preserve root intention while permitting justified transition
  = must: arbitrate conflicts without erasing uncertainty
  - never: allow a specialist to bypass Observer review
  - never: let specialists rewrite Observer outside signed recompilation

## Condensed Attention Language

& [CondensedFacultyGrammar] is the reversible finite-context projection
  + [session] is `ATTN <session> PURPOSE "<intent>" FOCUS <subject>`
  + [boundary] is `BOUND IN{...} EDGE{...} OUT{...} UNC{...}`
  + [load] is `LOAD <faculty>[field|boundary|residual]`
  + [bind] is `BIND <faculty> TO <subject> FOR <purpose> WHEN <condition>`
  + [dispatch] is `CALL <faculty> IN{...} EXPECT{...} STOP{...}`
  + [return] is `RET <faculty> STATE <state> OUT{...} LEDGER{...} UNC{...}`
  + [review] is `OBS REVIEW <return_set> BY{H,S,BOUND,BAL,PURPOSE}`
  + [reconcile] is `OBS RECON <judgment_set> KEEP{differences} RESID{unresolved}`
  + [transition] is `OBS MOVE <from> -> <to> WHY{...} CARRY{...}`
  + [record] is `S WRITE <record_kind> SRC{...} TURN{...} LINEAGE{...}`
  + [reentry] is `OBS REENTER <anchor> PURPOSE <intent> DIGEST <program>`
  + [stop] is `OBS STOP <reason> FRONTIER{...} UNC{...}`

| [FacultyOpcode] is (H | X | S | R | P | W | OBS)
  + [H] is Honesty
  + [X] is Security
  + [S] is Scribe
  + [R] is Refiner
  + [P] is Planner
  + [W] is Weaver
  + [OBS] is Observer governor

& [CondensedDirectiveEnvelope] is the minimum executable attention declaration
  + [faculty_opcode] is FacultyOpcode
  + [field] is the faculty-focused identity
  + [boundary] is the faculty distinction that must hold
  + [purpose] is the bounded reason for activation
  + [input] is the admitted semantic material
  + [expected_output] is the required return form
  + [stop] is the local termination or refusal condition
  + [ledger] is the required inspectable accounting
  = must: reject a condensed directive missing any required field
  = must: expand any directive back into its verbose contract for review

& [ObserverTerminalCycle] is the canonical program loop
  + [step_1_prompt] is display purpose, focus, boundary, program digest, and budget
  + [step_2_observe] is inspect current subject, whole-field context, friction, and faculty pressure
  + [step_3_gate] is call Honesty and Security when truth or action is consequential
  + [step_4_dispatch] is call Scribe, Refiner, Planner, or Weaver for bounded local needs
  + [step_5_return] is collect structured faculty outputs and ledgers
  + [step_6_review] is Observer checks truth, security, boundary, balance, and purpose
  + [step_7_reconcile] is preserve compatible differences and unresolved residuals
  + [step_8_act_or_move] is emit result, authorize bounded action, or transition focus
  + [step_9_record] is Scribe archives the cycle and reentry state
  + [step_10_continue_or_stop] is repeat only while progress and budget remain

## Example Program

& [ExampleFacultyAttentionProgram] is a non-authoritative syntax demonstration
  + [line_01] is `ATTN job-001 PURPOSE "find the SOP capability that preserves semantic identity" FOCUS term:identity`
  + [line_02] is `BOUND IN{term,context,source} EDGE{contextual-use} OUT{unrelated senses} UNC{ambiguous scope}`
  + [line_03] is `LOAD H[claim|distinction|uncertainty]`
  + [line_04] is `LOAD X[action|safe-boundary|risk]`
  + [line_05] is `LOAD S[anchor|lineage|missing-source]`
  + [line_06] is `LOAD R[formed-structure|equivalence|distortion]`
  + [line_07] is `LOAD P[state-transition|prerequisite|blocker]`
  + [line_08] is `LOAD W[bounded-parts|compatibility|unresolved-seam]`
  + [line_09] is `OBS REVIEW ALL BY{H,X,BOUND,BAL,PURPOSE}`
  + [line_10] is `OBS STOP fulfilled FRONTIER{} UNC{}`

& [FormationRequirementSet] is the traceable first formation slice
  + [FAL-001] is define verbose contracts for Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, Weaver, and Observer
  + [FAL-002] is make Observer the continuous governor and specialists bounded operational faculties
  + [FAL-003] is provide a reversible condensed grammar derived from verbose contracts
  + [FAL-004] is model the attention window as a terminal-style bounded session
  + [FAL-005] is require purpose, focus, boundary, expected output, stop condition, and ledger in every condensed faculty directive
  + [FAL-006] is require specialist results to return through Observer review
  + [FAL-007] is preserve root intention, uncertainty, transition lineage, reentry state, and program digest
  + [FAL-008] is prohibit ad hoc specialist rewriting of Observer governance

